-- title:
--   Integrality over A[̄ j] forces coefficients into A
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$) and let $M$ be a nonzero natural number. Consider the field $F_M =$ `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (modularFunctionFieldFull M)`, namely the subfield of the Laurent series field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((t))$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the coefficientwise images, under the map `coeffEmb` induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, of the elements of `modularFunctionFieldFull M`, itself the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((t))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the series `qExpand ℚ d jq` for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $M$. Let $e \in F_M$, and let `affineBaseFin M A` be the subring of $F_M$ generated by the image of $A$ under $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to F_M$ together with the single element `jBar M`, the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq`. Assume there is a monic polynomial with coefficients in `affineBaseFin M A` which, evaluated at $e$ via the inclusion of that subring into $F_M$, gives $0$. The conclusion is that the Laurent series underlying $e$ lies in `integralCoeffs A.toSubring`, that is, its coefficient at every integer index belongs to $A$.
--
--   This is the integral-closedness statement underlying the passage from modular functions to their Fourier coefficients: the subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((t))$ consisting of series with all coefficients in the valuation ring $A$ is integrally closed in the function field, so integrality over the affine coordinate ring $A[\bar j]$ already forces $A$-integrality of all coefficients. It is used throughout the construction of the characteristic-$p$ fibre model of the modular curve of level $M$, where coefficientwise reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ must be defined on elements integral over $A[\bar j]$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_mem_integralCoeffs_of_integral_affineBaseFin.lean

